data: {"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"data\": {\n    \"lookupStatus\": \"found\",\n    \"comments\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDoxOTA1NTA5NjI3MDc2NDgzXzE5MDU1MzUzMTM3NDA1ODE=\",\n        \"text\": \"You are absolutely not too late, especially for D2, D3, NAIA and JUCO. But going into senior year, it’s time to be very intentional.\\n\\nIf MSUB is your dream, go after it. Email the coaches directly, send updated video, your schedule, academics, measurables and specifically tell them why MSUB. Don’t eliminate yourself because you think you might not be “good enough”—let the coaches make that decision.\\n\\nAt the same time, broaden your list. Find schools at multiple levels that fit you academically, athletically and financially. Keep emailing, attend camps where the staff has shown interest, and don’t measure recruiting success by social-media follows or profile views.\\n\\nMost importantly: don’t panic and don’t give up. There are plenty of 2027s still looking for their opportunity. You only need one school and one coach who believes you fit their program.\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-27T02:39:28.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 5,\n        \"reactionCount\": 69,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Patrick Razz\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"1023978402\",\n          \"shortName\": \"Patrick\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDoxOTA1NTA5NjI3MDc2NDgzXzE5MDU1MTQ1MTM3NDI2NjE=\",\n        \"text\": \"If making MSUB doesn’t work out, you can always attend a JC with hopes of transferring in.  That would allow you 2 additional years of growth and development at the JC.\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-27T02:03:14.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 0,\n        \"reactionCount\": 16,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Michael Dilbeck\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"pfbid02PPVxQVmKMdJeB9rFkuGQYqbttv7Xf4KKjTUdwMV8dFXSeVJHQpQjhYzbYZwREtAVl\",\n          \"shortName\": \"Michael\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDoxOTA1NTA5NjI3MDc2NDgzXzE5MDU1MjAwNzcwNzU0Mzg=\",\n        \"text\": \"play JUCO and play 2 years and transfer in vs sitting\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-27T02:14:08.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 0,\n        \"reactionCount\": 58,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Darin Krueger\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"pfbid0jspJAwwCNp5uuFssoTjZTtUZtEfnN7JcrwJmtuVT5JqGyrR5YLCW8wSRCj1dgaMRl\",\n          \"shortName\": \"Darin\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDoxOTA1NTA5NjI3MDc2NDgzXzE5MDU1MTIwODM3NDI5MDQ=\",\n        \"text\": \"You are not too late, email, post,email again. Keep on going, work hard and cast a huge net!!!! training, game footage etc.\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-27T01:58:44.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 0,\n        \"reactionCount\": 3,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Korena Gutierrez\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"pfbid0HXXhCpB4mxCY9DQjGtcKQdSRUnQ7JQec1ySH4EDDmZZ3YsFPecFsjjuLHV4rs8Kwl\",\n          \"shortName\": \"Korena\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDoxOTA1NTA5NjI3MDc2NDgzXzE5MDU1MTQyMTcwNzYwMjQ=\",\n        \"text\": \"Send me your clips kdavis@uftl.edu\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-27T02:02:36.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 0,\n        \"reactionCount\": 26,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Kyle Davis\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"pfbid02utNmh7CxAH27BrwXxSneaWeK9adbnAKGnqARAQTLEa7GbfF9yjZjkHfyjopWrLQpl\",\n          \"shortName\": \"Kyle\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDoxOTA1NTA5NjI3MDc2NDgzXzE5MDc4NTQyNDM1MDg2ODg=\",\n        \"text\": \"Hey Emily.  My daughter plays at MSUb.   They did get a new coach and AD.  I’m sure there is so much she’s having to prepare for beings she’s new and also moving in so maybe emails are getting missed.\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-29T17:20:28.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 2,\n        \"reactionCount\": 1,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Haley LaFond Gray\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"pfbid0BtZ962VqEdvYJevqpDSC4yKkmMgQcTxkLgdUjMKaMnnr6cDEv24kcknYazCTYu5Kl\",\n          \"shortName\": \"Haley\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDoxOTA1NTA5NjI3MDc2NDgzXzE5MDYzNzYzOTM2NTY0NzM=\",\n        \"text\": \"First, don't doubt your self kid! You got this! Keep believing and reach out to more then one school. If you dream it then it is possible. Life is all about the experience and if you want it bad enough you can make it happen. Stay strong you got this.\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-28T01:34:03.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 1,\n        \"reactionCount\": 1,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Ben Belote\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"pfbid032k1YV2CNMSvaQ5rtf6ZGLfGxToWsr4dLVDEn1KDXFKyGSn3e5R3QZxmrtarg2hjFl\",\n          \"shortName\": \"Ben\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDoxOTA1NTA5NjI3MDc2NDgzXzE5MDU1MTYyNjM3NDI0ODY=\",\n        \"text\": \"Keep working hard, never give up on your goals. Stay focus and committed on & off the field. Go to camps to get some feedback from college coaches. Be realistic with your expectations but don’t sell yourself short. Best of luck\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-27T02:06:56.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 0,\n        \"reactionCount\": 6,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Bobby Antillon\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"pfbid07BXee82AUGjkAvzb1KrFdkpY9fX8bamayLu8v9gZ1aG3pmQt6efqGtcrk74uF2UTl\",\n          \"shortName\": \"Bobby\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDoxOTA1NTA5NjI3MDc2NDgzXzE5MDU1Mzk2MDA0MDY4MTk=\",\n        \"text\": \"First thing to do is to contact Tommy Davis, he’s out of Texas and has helped many Student Athletes during their softball journey. Great person, great coach, has many College contacts nation wide and cares about the players he works with!!!\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-27T02:45:46.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 2,\n        \"reactionCount\": 10,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Christopher Hendricks\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"pfbid04twyMKQsGd8nToPA9Ydcqb3KbQU1KomuBd87iAuuQshELBDmEr9y5yj1JswwfLLKl\",\n          \"shortName\": \"Christopher\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDoxOTA1NTA5NjI3MDc2NDgzXzE5MDU1MTQ2ODA0MDkzMTE=\",\n        \"text\": \"Make a field level account and X account. Email the coaches of the schools you want to go to and also see when they are offering camps for those specific schools. The big camps with 50 coaches is a money maker.\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-27T02:03:35.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 2,\n        \"reactionCount\": 6,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Stacey Leo\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"pfbid0Yr4dhihRzEzFBKB1wXdFaEx8pGm4wAtB5vgtR9xeEh9R6c81K7PEULkTiR4APDiJl\",\n          \"shortName\": \"Stacey\"\n        }\n      }\n    ],\n    \"page\": {\n      \"nextCursor\": \"MToxNzkzOTg0NTgyOgF_G9bQaZIxRKlhB57OmR28VZS1VL6Lr908kQOGe6ueSsc-0xMqB7xGKB73v2GtiJWGntfy8VgRKbinhID3k3INBFgCWiIHZ8ZGvSgAWLcompZ3sDeky7ncsPon2rh9uR6lQexVOq4lSrbFiVi26WgPZer701Tl9UDiaLqRTy2_wa-1TI0rqq-7pJ-Y1HMsnVb4-tKzstBNnGekHrfMJw71jNjXBMTvnEO_rniVcBaibglFl6XJk6gCv46ivKWNmh1Hy5Vz11TcG-AMh-hkU0ctaV98Mcw3toJ7spKZIR5YbH-2OP_cWqVl44AsVZWpG2ITznsOK6sqRV5daCdxzTa3gjvN-gyF917Xmj5l9vAc-nNUBUuzGqMPJt-lcT1r9P1keobWDfePIfY_bQgNjoCB6SKsGRtGp3JDhE-me-hAmfbdnV022jgzhKI\",\n      \"hasMore\": true\n    }\n  },\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"requestId\": \"req_7df4dd61-5457-439c-84d6-3999fe9b96dd\",\n    \"creditsCharged\": 1,\n    \"version\": \"v1\"\n  }\n}"},{"type":"text","text":"{\"conversation_id\":\"01a1b1d0-1acf-7780-96ab-caa7e6da49d2\"}"}],"structuredContent":{"data":{"lookupStatus":"found","comments":[{"id":"Y29tbWVudDoxOTA1NTA5NjI3MDc2NDgzXzE5MDU1MzUzMTM3NDA1ODE=","text":"You are absolutely not too late, especially for D2, D3, NAIA and JUCO. But going into senior year, it’s time to be very intentional.\n\nIf MSUB is your dream, go after it. Email the coaches directly, send updated video, your schedule, academics, measurables and specifically tell them why MSUB. Don’t eliminate yourself because you think you might not be “good enough”—let the coaches make that decision.\n\nAt the same time, broaden your list. Find schools at multiple levels that fit you academically, athletically and financially. Keep emailing, attend camps where the staff has shown interest, and don’t measure recruiting success by social-media follows or profile views.\n\nMost importantly: don’t panic and don’t give up. There are plenty of 2027s still looking for their opportunity. You only need one school and one coach who believes you fit their program.","createdAt":"2026-08-27T02:39:28.000Z","replyCount":5,"reactionCount":69,"repliesCursor":"","author":{"name":"Patrick Razz","platformUserId":"1023978402","shortName":"Patrick"}},{"id":"Y29tbWVudDoxOTA1NTA5NjI3MDc2NDgzXzE5MDU1MTQ1MTM3NDI2NjE=","text":"If making MSUB doesn’t work out, you can always attend a JC with hopes of transferring in.  That would allow you 2 additional years of growth and development at the JC.","createdAt":"2026-08-27T02:03:14.000Z","replyCount":0,"reactionCount":16,"repliesCursor":"","author":{"name":"Michael Dilbeck","platformUserId":"pfbid02PPVxQVmKMdJeB9rFkuGQYqbttv7Xf4KKjTUdwMV8dFXSeVJHQpQjhYzbYZwREtAVl","shortName":"Michael"}},{"id":"Y29tbWVudDoxOTA1NTA5NjI3MDc2NDgzXzE5MDU1MjAwNzcwNzU0Mzg=","text":"play JUCO and play 2 years and transfer in vs sitting","createdAt":"2026-08-27T02:14:08.000Z","replyCount":0,"reactionCount":58,"r